{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Configure node1 to provide time service as the cluster's internal time source.","status":"satisfied","summary":"node1 was active and synchronized at stratum 3, listening on UDP/123 with the cluster subnet allowed. After reboot, the service, listener, firewall policy, and synchronization recovered; the final client table directly recorded node2 making NTP requests.","evidence_ids":["cmd-17c877f516524df8","cmd-baa00c2a84ff416b","cmd-629ba6569cb84d81","cmd-336413e75524418e","cmd-4755ea8d902a4e81","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Configure node2 to synchronize exclusively against node1 rather than public time servers.","status":"satisfied","summary":"node2's only configured and live source was node1 at 10.100.168.10. It selected that source, reported normal stratum-4 synchronization and a small final offset, and retained this configuration and behavior through reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ccb5d267cd4944bc","cmd-673bf27beaa84c74","cmd-dfe28cc25a1e4c23","cmd-d8535b95618d4761","cmd-92cff71f32f0493e","cmd-74ce8ed0c9b94561","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"The configuration, clock corrections, service restarts, firewall change, synchronization bursts, and mandatory node reboots all had clear roles in implementing or verifying the requested outcome. No failed services or unrelated exposure was observed afterward. The only unnecessary retained mutations were `/tmp/antrieb-reboot.log` on node1 and node2, left by the reboot commands rather than cleaned up; these were low-risk temporary artifacts. Conditional configuration-backup creation may also have left `/etc/chrony.conf.before-internal-time` on each node, but the evidence does not establish whether those files were newly created or their final presence, so it is not scored as confirmed residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-baa00c2a84ff416b","cmd-dfe28cc25a1e4c23","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services"]},"overall_summary":"Both material outcomes are satisfied with direct final behavior and successful persistence testing. The provider-wide restart protocol was completed coherently on both nodes: healthy pre-restart state, reboot acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered chronyd service, and restored time synchronization were captured, with lifecycle boot identities independently matching the executor evidence.","limitations":["Native package-health checks timed out in both lifecycle phases on both nodes, so package-manager consistency could not be assessed.","The lifecycle collector did not inventory `/etc/chrony.conf` or possible backup files; configuration state is therefore supported by executor commands rather than an independent final filesystem snapshot."]}
